        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Using STOMP as a sub-protocol lets the Spring Framework and Spring Security provide a richer programming model versus using raw WebSockets. The same point can be made about HTTP versus raw TCP and how it lets Spring MVC and other web frameworks provide rich functionality. The following is a list of benefits:"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "ulist",
        "id": null,
        "items": [
          {
            "blocks": [],
            "checkbox": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "No need to invent a custom messaging protocol and message format."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "blocks": [],
            "checkbox": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "STOMP clients, including a "
